## Resolved mutable: wasm-jit-feasible

webix AGENTS.md:93-94 (witnessed by the user, test.js 19/19): "JIT impossible. Blinks JIT emits native x86-64/aarch64 only; under wasm32 it is structurally impossible. NOJIT is permanent in-browser." REASON: wasm is a sandbox - you cannot mmap(PROT_EXEC) and run runtime-generated NATIVE bytes. Blinks JIT copies compiled C micro-op bodies (native machine code) at runtime; that technique cannot target the wasm sandbox. THE ONLY way to do runtime codegen in wasm is to EMIT WASM BYTECODE and WebAssembly.instantiate() it - a different JIT backend nobody has written for blink. Such a wasm-emitting dynarec is theoretically possible but: (a) instantiate() is async + has per-module overhead (kills tiny hot paths), (b) is a large new engineering effort, (c) still slower than native JIT. CONCLUSION: cannot make blinks EXISTING jit run in wasm; could in principle BUILD a wasm-emitting jit backend, but it is a major project with uncertain realtime payoff. For now NOJIT interpreter is the ceiling.